hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16052","He said, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar al-Abdi, from his father, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until tribes are swallowed by the earth, and it is said, who remains of Banu so-and-so. He said, so I knew when he said tribes that they are the Arabs, because the non-Arabs are attributed to their villages."
"16053","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said, and al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Rahman ibn Suhar al-Abdi narrated to us, from his father, he said, I sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to permit me a jar to make nabidh in, and he allowed me it, or permitted me it."
